5025-> FIX: TWO scratch words. A one-word role-aware guard is MEASURABLY WRONG for
5026-> `str pc,[pc,#imm]`, where arg[0] and arg[2] are the same pointer and setting
5027:> the base to +8 silently moves the STORED word to +8 — which A2-9 :1637-1641
5028-> forbids, since an implementation may pick +8 or +12 for R15 stores but must
5029-> use ONE everywhere. cpu_arm.h gains tmp_pc_data[2]; both decoder sites point
5030-> arg[2] at it; the store arm computes both values unconditionally. Separating
5031-> the roles at DECODE time removes any run-time pointer-identity test, and the
5032-> [2] sizing keeps a doubleword's second word off tmp_branch (THUMB state).
